   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Said as kutsu haite (put your shoes on) at the door; casual speech drops o. haiteru means already has them on, not 'putting them on now'.",
   "notes": "Spelled like haku 'throw up' and haku 'sweep', but the pitch differs: haku 'put on' is flat (ha-KU), the other two fall after ha (HA-ku). Context helps too.",
