  {
   "id": "c-fuku-o-nugu",
   "romaji": "fuku o nugu",
   "polite": "fuku o nugimasu",
   "english": "take off clothes, get undressed",
   "ja": "服を脱ぐ",
   "kana": "ふくをぬぐ",
   "politeJa": "服を脱ぎます",
   "noun": "fuku",
   "particle": "o",
   "verb": "nugu",
   "verbJa": "脱ぐ",
   "verbSense": "take off (clothes, shoes)",
   "englishVerb": "take off",
   "trap": "Not fuku o toru, which sounds like picking clothes up (fuku totte = pass me my clothes). Whatever goes on with kiru or haku (tops, trousers, shoes, socks) comes off with nugu. A hat comes off with toru or nugu. Glasses, masks, watches, ties and belts come off with hazusu, and casual toru works for most of them.",
