    "uwagi (jacket)",
    "kooto (coat)",
    "seetaa (sweater)",
    "kutsushita (socks)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Heard as nuide (take them off) or nuida hou ga ii (you'd better take them off), and ofuku nuide (with the o- used to children) is what kids hear at bath time. When it's one layer, people name it: uwagi nuidara? (why not take your jacket off?). Casual speech drops o.",
   "notes": "Once it's clear which garment, nugu alone is enough: atsui kara nuijaou (it's hot, I'll take it off).",
